#DESCRIPTION
Zero-current hybrid-PIC wave test.

The domain is seeded with a sinusoidal magnetic-field perturbation riding on a
uniform guide field Bx0 (set via the generic WaveIC plug-in, selected with the
waveic test-case command).
Crucially, NO macroparticles are loaded (nParticle per cell = 0 0 0), so the ion
charge/mass density rho is identically zero everywhere. In the hybrid field
solver the generalized Ohm's law is fully short-circuited by the rho > 0 guard,
so every cell is left inert and contributes no electric field, i.e. E = 0.
Faraday's law then gives dB/dt = -curl E = 0: the B perturbation is FROZEN and
does NOT propagate. (Physically this is the zero-current regime -- with no plasma
there is no current source to drive the field. Mechanically it is the rho = 0
inert-cell path, not a literal J = 0 inside the Hall formula: the sinusoidal B
itself has curl B not equal to zero, but the Hall term is simply never evaluated
because rho is zero.)

The validation requires the magnetic energy Eb to be conserved AND the electric
field energy Ee to stay at ~0 -- the genuine signature that the field is frozen
rather than merely energy-conserving (a non-dispersive propagating wave would
also conserve Eb, but would have Ee greater than zero).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall term ON (this test confirms it is silent when J = 0 / rho = 0).
#HALLTERM
T                       useHallTerm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); no particles are actually loaded below.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

Uniform guide field Bx0 along x.
#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   (ignored: no particles loaded)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

Sinusoidal transverse B perturbation along x. With zero particles E stays 0 so
this perturbation does not propagate (Hall term vanishes because J = 0). The wave
sub-parameters are set in the wave initial-condition command block (value-first
SWMF convention: value then name), read by the WaveIC plug-in through
ReadParam::read_optional. The block must list its sub-parameters in the same order
they are read in WaveIC::read_param; omitted ones keep the generic preset
defaults.
#TESTCASE
waveic

#WAVEIC
1       seedB
1       guideField
1       waveMode
0.5     frac

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

NO macroparticles: rho = 0 everywhere => cells inert => E = 0 => B frozen.
#PARTICLES
0                       nParticle per cell in X
0                       nParticle per cell in Y
0                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
6.25                    TimeMax   frozen-field window (E = 0, B static)

#RUN
